cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Research prototype on synthetic benchmarks, not a peer-reviewed publication. Please also cite the methods listed in README.md."
title: "Noise-aware active equation discovery"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jiang
    given-names: Haoyang
version: 0.2.0
abstract: "One first-order noise model, Cov(r) = sigma^2 J J^T, used both to identify sparse equations (whitening and a significance test) and to choose the next experiment (I-optimal on whitened rows). Compared with Active E-SINDy, D-optimal design and literature identifiers given active selection, on point, trajectory, PDE, domain-model and network-dynamics protocols."
keywords:
  - equation discovery
  - SINDy
  - active learning
  - optimal experimental design
